  "version": "1.1.0",
  "description": {
    "en": "AX0-COUNTERS (docs/research/2026-10-02-ax-implementation-plan.md §A0, + card W-AX0 (e)). Each venue's Durable Object counts, in memory, for the life of one wake: (a) ?since= catch-ups and how many the window could not answer (since_total/since_none); (b) whether this window holds the wake and the wake has written nothing yet (wakes_total/wakes_readonly), plus the wake's own reads/writes (never flushed); (c) the wall of each orders fold from bytes (cold_folds, cold_fold_us, up to 16 samples, the first after the wake); (d) chunks stored per write (proj_rows/writes); (e) per catalogue write: bytes of the two Catalog::load decodes, the edit journal's bytes, and the wall of each part. GET /api/owner/health returns them as `counters`; ?counters=flush (the nightly) answers AND zeroes, so summed nights count nothing twice. Nothing is stored: a hibernation erases an unflushed window, and the next window says cause=wake so the collector sees the gap. CLOCK: on the platform Date.now only advances after I/O (developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/performance, Apr 23 2026), so a live cat_decode_us is ~0 by construction and only the byte counts and the I/O spans are real; natively the µs are real (clock=native-us). v1.1.0 (W-AE, 2026-10-07): adds the optional `ae` object -- the Analytics Engine writer's own state for this wake (binding name, points accepted, refusals, the last refusal's text); the points themselves are contract feature-ae-counters.json.",
    "uk": "Лічильники об'єкта закладу (AX0): опитування ?since= без відповіді, пробудження лише з читанням, холодна згортка, рядки на запис і вартість запису каталогу; /api/owner/health -> counters, ?counters=flush обнуляє."
  },
